# Vendored converter inputs from Unihan 18.0.0 (2026-07-31), fetched from
# https://www.unicode.org/Public/UCD/latest/ucd/Unihan.zip
#
# Only the three files hunmin reads are kept:
#   - Unihan_Readings.txt      kDefinition (English gloss per Hanja)
#   - Unihan_Variants.txt      kTraditionalVariant (simplified-form detection)
#   - Unihan_OtherMappings.txt kJoyoKanji, kJinmeiyoKanji (Japanese),
#                               kKoreanEducationHanja, kKoreanName (Korean use)
#
# SHA256SUMS pins the exact bytes; tools/hanja2data.py records these hashes in
# the generated hunmin.data meta so provenance cannot drift (the same rule the
# libhangul inputs already follow). Do not hand-edit these files: regenerate by
# re-downloading Unihan.zip and re-running hanja2data.py's selfcheck.
